  "label": "Hitler is Anne Frankly",
  "description": "The text 'anne frankly' is mapped onto Adolf Hitler, creating an analogical mapping where Hitler is being portrayed as Anne Frank, or more precisely, as the person who is 'Anne Frankly' (a pun on 'Anne Frank' and 'annoyingly frankly'). This mapping is ironic and hateful, as it juxtaposes the perpetrator of the Holocaust with the victim whose diary is referenced, implying a false equivalence or mocking the gravity of her suffering. The visual material (Adolf Hitler) is mapped onto the textual material ('anne frankly') to create this provocative and offensive statement.",
